@format 1
@id media-loading.in-worklist
@title In Worklist
@section Media loading
@area In Worklist
@entry worklist-relay, delivered-output, clear-tabs, relay-source-remove, batch-evict
@summary Show Worklist delivery/relay operations with their actual direct LDocketPathsAdd and LDocketPathsRemove calls, including forced source removal at the Finish target.
@related media-loading.common.docket-insertion, media-loading.common.docket-removal, media-loading.common.workspace-media-clear, media-loading.in-staged-workspace
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag worklist

@alias roster = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PRoster
@alias list = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PList
@alias console = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PConsole
@alias strip = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.PStrip
@alias docket = Cadroue.Application.LDocket
@alias cartographer = Cadroue.ShellEngine.LCartographer

[worklist-relay] Worklist relay to tab <input>
- Require a target Files docket, then select the target tab before replacing its unlocked Files paths @ roster.PRosterRelaySend(...)
> worklist-target

[delivered-output] Delivered processing output <input>
- Resolve the requested destination/original tab and its Files docket in PListDeliveredAdd or PListDeliveredPlace @ list.PListDeliveredAdd(...)
  @ list.PListDeliveredPlace(...)
> delivered-target

[clear-tabs] Worklist Clear Tabs command <input>
- After destructive confirmation, call PStripContentClear, which invokes PWorkspaceMediaClear for every tab workspace @ console.PConsoleTabsHandle(...)
  @ strip.PStripContentClear(...)
> map:media-loading.common.workspace-media-clear

[relay-source-remove] Post-delivery source-drop request <input>
- LCartographerDeliver requests ordinary source drop with force=false after successful tab/stage delivery, but requests force=true when the relay target is Finish @ cartographer.LCartographerDeliver(...)
- PListDeliveredRemove receives that force flag with the delivered work item @ list.PListDeliveredRemove(...)
> source-remove-gate

[batch-evict] Worklist batch eviction <input>
- Find docket entries whose batches left the Worklist and call LDocketPathsRemove for those paths; matching Merge group paths are removed afterward @ list.PListBatchEvict(...)
> map:media-loading.common.docket-removal

[worklist-target] Worklist target availability <decision>
- Continue only when the target exposes a Files docket @ roster.PRosterRelaySend(...)
? "Target Files docket available" > target-clear-check
? "Target unavailable" > worklist-rejected

[delivered-target] Delivery target availability <decision>
- Continue only when the destination/original tab still exposes a Files docket @ list.PListDeliveredAdd(...)
  @ list.PListDeliveredPlace(...)
? "Target Files docket available" > delivered-scan
? "Target unavailable" > delivery-rejected

[source-remove-gate] Source removal policy <decision>
- PListDeliveredRemove skips only when removal is not forced and Relay Empty is disabled; a forced request bypasses the Relay Empty preference @ list.PListDeliveredRemove(...)
? "Forced, or Relay Empty enabled" > source-tab-check
? "Not forced and Relay Empty disabled" > source-kept

[target-clear-check] Existing unlocked target paths <decision>
- Read all unlocked target entries before the relay insertion @ roster.PRosterRelaySend(...)
? "Unlocked target paths exist" > target-remove
? "Nothing to clear" > target-no-remove

[worklist-rejected] Worklist relay rejected <output>
= No target Files removal or insertion occurs.

[delivered-scan] Scan delivered path directly <process>
- Scan the single delivered output with PListMediaScan, then pass the result directly to LDocketPathsAdd with the supplied batch and delivered=true; PListPathsAdd is not called @ list.PListMediaScan(...)
  @ docket.LDocketPathsAdd(...)
> map:media-loading.common.docket-insertion

[delivery-rejected] Delivered output rejected <output>
= No target docket insertion occurs.

[source-tab-check] Source tab still available <decision>
- Resolve the source tab recorded by the work item; no Files/group removal can occur when that tab is gone @ list.PListDeliveredRemove(...)
? "Source tab found" > source-paths
? "Source tab gone" > source-gone

[source-kept] Source retained by policy <output>
= Ordinary delivery leaves the source and merge-source paths in their source tab when Relay Empty is disabled.

[target-remove] Synchronous target docket removal <process>
- Call LDocketPathsRemove for every unlocked target path; the complete Common / Docket removal callback chain runs synchronously before PRosterRelaySend resumes @ roster.PRosterRelaySend(...)
  @ docket.LDocketPathsRemove(...)
! The target tab was selected before removal, so a replacement PListPathChange can reach an active viewer; PListClearChange can then force-close that viewer as shown in Common / Docket removal.
> target-after-remove

[target-no-remove] Target already clear <junction>
> target-after-remove

[source-paths] Build delivered source path set <process>
- Build the removal set from the work item's primary source plus all merge-source paths @ list.PListDeliveredRemove(...)
> source-docket-remove

[source-gone] Source removal unavailable <output>
= The source tab no longer exists, so PListDeliveredRemove changes no source Files or Merge grouping state.

[target-after-remove] Relay removal branches converge <junction>
> relay-scan

[source-docket-remove] Remove source Files entries <process>
- Call LDocketPathsRemove on the source tab's Files docket when present; its synchronous Files/viewer consequences are the shared Common / Docket removal behavior @ list.PListDeliveredRemove(...)
  @ docket.LDocketPathsRemove(...)
! See Common / Docket removal for replacement selection and possible viewer/flow clearing.
> source-group-remove

[relay-scan] Scan relay paths directly <process>
- Scan relay paths with PListMediaScan, create a new batch, and pass the scanned paths directly to LDocketPathsAdd; PListPathsAdd is not called @ list.PListMediaScan(...)
  @ docket.LDocketPathsAdd(...)
> map:media-loading.common.docket-insertion

[source-group-remove] Remove matching Merge grouping paths <process>
- After Files removal, remove the same source/merge-source paths from the source tab's Merge group when that surface exists @ list.PListDeliveredRemove(...)
> source-removed

[source-removed] Delivered source removal completed <output>
= The source Files and applicable Merge grouping paths have been offered for removal. A forced Finish-target drop performs this path even when Relay Empty is disabled.
